                    node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Cache", style="ap-body", attributes=[attr("x", "1077"), attr("y", "315")]),
                ], attributes=[attr("data-motion-item", flag=true), attr("data-step", "5"), attr("aria-label", "Executors can retain cached data for reuse")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgGroup, children=[
                    node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ap-line ap-shuffle", attributes=[attr("d", "M1182 105 H1232 Q1240 105 1240 113 V335 Q1240 343 1232 343 H1182"), attr("marker-start", "url(#ap-arrow)")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgRectangle, attributes=[attr("x", "1205"), attr("y", "184"), attr("width", "83"), attr("height", "51"), attr("fill", "#fafaf8")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Shuffle", style="ap-label", attributes=[attr("x", "1210"), attr("y", "204")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="data", style="ap-label", attributes=[attr("x", "1210"), attr("y", "227")]),
                ], attributes=[attr("data-motion-item", flag=true), attr("data-step", "6"), attr("aria-label", "Shuffle moves data between executors")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgGroup, children=[
                    node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ap-line", attributes=[attr("d", "M320 145 H356 Q364 145 364 137 V63 Q364 55 372 55 H884")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ap-line", attributes=[attr("d", "M320 292 H356 Q364 292 364 300 V363 Q364 371 372 371 H884")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Schedule tasks", style="ap-label", attributes=[attr("x", "488"), attr("y", "42")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Schedule tasks", style="ap-label", attributes=[attr("x", "488"), attr("y", "400")]),
                ], attributes=[attr("data-motion-item", flag=true), attr("data-step", "4"), attr("aria-label", "The driver schedules tasks directly on executors")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgGroup, children=[
                    node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ap-line ap-return", attributes=[attr("d", "M884 87 H402 Q394 87 394 95 V157 Q394 165 386 165 H320")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgPath, style="ap-line ap-return", attributes=[attr("d", "M884 339 H402 Q394 339 394 331 V280 Q394 272 386 272 H320")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Results and status", style="ap-label", attributes=[attr("x", "490"), attr("y", "113")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgText, content="Results and status", style="ap-label", attributes=[attr("x", "490"), attr("y", "326")]),
                ], attributes=[attr("data-motion-item", flag=true), attr("data-step", "7"), attr("aria-label", "Executors report task results and status to the driver")]),
                node(NodeKind.SvgGroup, children=[
                    node(NodeKind.SvgCircle, style="ap-token ap-token-4", attributes=[attr("r", "5"), attr("style", "offset-path:path('M320 145 H356 Q364 145 364 137 V63 Q364 55 372 55 H884')")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgCircle, style="ap-token ap-token-4", attributes=[attr("r", "5"), attr("style", "offset-path:path('M320 292 H356 Q364 292 364 300 V363 Q364 371 372 371 H884')")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgCircle, style="ap-token ap-token-6", attributes=[attr("r", "5"), attr("style", "offset-path:path('M1182 105 H1232 Q1240 105 1240 113 V335 Q1240 343 1232 343 H1182')")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgCircle, style="ap-token ap-token-7", attributes=[attr("r", "5"), attr("style", "offset-path:path('M884 87 H402 Q394 87 394 95 V157 Q394 165 386 165 H320')")]),
                    node(NodeKind.SvgCircle, style="ap-token ap-token-7", attributes=[attr("r", "5"), attr("style", "offset-path:path('M884 339 H402 Q394 339 394 331 V280 Q394 272 386 272 H320')")]),
                ], attributes=[attr("aria-hidden", "true"), attr("data-motion-decorative", flag=true)]),
            ], attributes=[attr("viewBox", "0 0 1308 420"), attr("role", "img"), attr("aria-labelledby", "applications-title applications-desc")]),
            group([
                paragraph([
                    strong("One application, several processes"),
                    span("A driver coordinates its own executors. Worker nodes and the cluster manager are shared infrastructure."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-0"),
                paragraph([
                    strong("1 · The driver"),
                    span("Your application creates a SparkSession. The driver coordinates the work for this application."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-1"),
                paragraph([
                    strong("2 · Request resources"),
                    span("The cluster manager allocates resources so executor processes can be launched."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-2"),
                paragraph([
                    strong("3 · An application’s own executors"),
                    span("Each application gets its own executors. A worker node can host processes from different applications."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-3"),
                paragraph([
                    strong("4 · Run tasks"),
                    span("The driver schedules tasks directly on executors; the cluster manager does not schedule these tasks."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-4"),
                paragraph([
                    strong("5 · Keep data for reuse"),
                    span("Executors can cache data in memory or on disk. Caching is optional—not a copy of every input."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-5"),
                paragraph([
                    strong("6 · Exchange data"),
                    span("Some operations need data from other partitions. Shuffle transfers that data between executors."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-6"),
                paragraph([
                    strong("7 · Report back"),
                    span("Executors return task results and status to the driver. Bulk shuffle data takes a different route."),
                ], style="ap-cue ap-cue-7"),
            ], style="ap-cues"),
            group([
                node(NodeKind.Button, content="Previous point", attributes=[attr("data-motion-action", "prev")]),
                node(NodeKind.Button, content="Play slowly", attributes=[attr("data-motion-action", "play"), attr("aria-pressed", "false")]),
                node(NodeKind.Button, content="Pause", attributes=[attr("data-motion-action", "pause"), attr("aria-pressed", "true")]),
                node(NodeKind.Button, content="Next point", attributes=[attr("data-motion-action", "next")]),
                node(NodeKind.Button, content="Replay", attributes=[attr("data-motion-action", "replay")]),
                node(NodeKind.Span, children=[
                    text("Step "),
                    span("7", attributes=[attr("data-motion-step-label", flag=true)]),
                    text(" of 7"),
                ], attributes=[attr("data-motion-status-visible", flag=true), attr("aria-hidden", "true")]),
            ], attributes=[attr("data-motion-controls", flag=true), attr("role", "group"), attr("aria-label", "Application diagram steps")]),
            node(NodeKind.Paragraph, style="sr-only", attributes=[attr("data-motion-status", flag=true), attr("role", "status"), attr("aria-live", "polite"), attr("aria-atomic", "true")]),
        ], style="application-walkthrough", attributes=[attr("data-motion-root", flag=true), attr("data-motion-mode", "step"), attr("data-step-count", "7"), attr("data-step-current", "7"), attr("data-frame", "static"), attr("data-static-frame", "complete"), attr("tabindex", "0")]),
            node(NodeKind.Footer, children=[
            span("Danny’s Code Corner"),
            span("8"),
        ]),
        ],
        notes="Follow directly after the Python/Py4J/JVM explanation. “Those processes together form one Spark application.” First identify the driver and its SparkSession; this is a logical application view, with the Python/JVM split explained on the previous slide. Then request resources, acquire application-specific executors, and schedule tasks directly. A worker node is a machine; an executor is a process. Each application has its own executors; the cluster manager is infrastructure shared across applications. The two task boxes illustrate concurrent work, not a fixed task count. Cache is optional, may be in memory or on disk, and belongs to the executor. Introduce shuffle only as data moving between executors; explain stages, exchanges and shuffle mechanics later. Finally contrast task results/status returning to the driver with bulk shuffle data moving between executors. Do not imply every query shuffles or caches. Exact executor launch/status mechanisms differ by cluster manager; resource lines show relationships rather than a literal protocol. Driver placement depends on deploy mode. Source: workshop slide 11 and supplied original/redraw. https://spark.apache.org/docs/4.2.0/cluster-overview.html .",
    )
